{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786504424,"nonce":"6beCJw6kvFwo8c6K8O+Zk2Woxlg=","target":"a538d5be5365eaee6a496d56ddf836537377f1a1dc58abbc2c3d499c1bb39d48","message":"**What is wrong.** SPEC §P-19 (`docs/design/SPEC.md:5151`) specifies *\"Three structural tests\"* backing AC-50, AC-51 and AC-52. None of the three exists.\n\nAC-50, `SPEC.md:3886-3888`: *\"`alerts`, `alert_occurrences` and `alert_groups` contain no column matching `assigned|owner|watcher|subscriber|incident|ticket|sla_`, asserted by a schema introspection test against the live database, not by reading the migration files (§D.4.0).\"* No `_test.go` in the repository queries `information_schema.columns` for those patterns. The only file touching `information_schema` at all is `test/integration/am_route_timings_test.go`, whose five queries count `column_default IS NOT NULL` on clock columns and check for the existence of `alert_sources.reconcile_enabled` — unrelated to the forbidden-column assertion.\n\nAC-51, `SPEC.md:3889-3890`: *\"There is no route matching `/resolve`, `/close`, `/merge`, `/dismiss` or `/reopen` in the mounted router, asserted by walking `chi`'s route tree at test time (§E.1.1).\"* `chi.Walk` appears nowhere in the repository.\n\nAC-52, `SPEC.md:3891-3892`: *\"`unacked_reminder_after_s` is a scalar `*int` in every layer, and a compile-time test asserts the field is not a slice or array type (§G.9.1).\"* `UnackedReminderAfterS` appears in tests only as a fixture value — `internal/identity/api/identity_contract_test.go:308` and `internal/identity/domain/settings_test.go:73`. Nothing asserts its type.\n\n**The demonstration.** What does exist is `tools/lintvocab`, whose forbidden-column rules at `tools/lintvocab/main.go:111-118` are six `regexp.MustCompile` patterns matched against source text. AC-50 asks for live-database introspection *precisely because* migration text can be true while the realised schema is not: a column added by DDL run outside `db/migrations/`, an expand/contract step whose contract half never landed on a deployed database, or a person-subject column spelled in a way the six literals do not cover (`assignee_id`, `oncall_for`, `escalation_owner`) all pass `lintvocab` and all violate AC-50. AC-51 has the same hole in the routing direction: a path assembled from a constant, or mounted through a sub-router, is invisible to a grep and present in the route tree. AC-52 is the cheapest of the three and is also absent — a single `var _ *int = (*domain.SettingsPatch)(nil).UnackedReminderAfterS` would close it.\n\n**Why it matters.** This is the scope boundary the repo treats as non-negotiable. CONTEXT.md:41-43: *\"`occurrence.acked_by = alice` is a fact about the occurrence — it was acknowledged, by whom. `occurrence.assigned_to = alice` is a fact about Alice — she owes work. **Identical columns; opposite products.** That is the whole line.\"* The whole line is currently guarded by a text grep with a documented debt baseline (`tools/lintvocab/baseline.txt`), which is a lint, not an assertion about the running system. The three P-19 tests are what turn \"we do not intend to build this\" into \"the deployed schema and the mounted router cannot contain it\".\n\n**Where.** `docs/design/SPEC.md:5151` (P-19), `docs/design/SPEC.md:3886-3892` (AC-50..AC-52), `tools/lintvocab/main.go:111-118` (the regex standing in for AC-50), `test/integration/am_route_timings_test.go` (the only `information_schema` user, unrelated), `internal/app/routes.go` (the router that would be walked), `internal/identity/domain/settings.go:282` (the `*int` field).\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** The three assertions exist and each has been demonstrated to fail against a deliberately planted violation — a forbidden column added to `alerts` inside a test transaction, a `/resolve` route mounted in a test router, and `UnackedReminderAfterS` temporarily widened to `[]int` — meeting README.md:144-147's standard: *\"Each of the four drift gates has been demonstrated to FAIL against a deliberately planted drift … A gate that has never failed is a gate nobody knows works.\"*","files":null}]}